00:14:15,720 --> 00:14:17,320
For playing out loud.

269
00:14:18,700 --> 00:14:20,680
Where did that dumb girl run off to?

270
00:14:20,840 --> 00:14:21,540
Hey!

271
00:14:22,000 --> 00:14:23,040
Icarus!

272
00:14:23,420 --> 00:14:24,240
Stop yelling.

273
00:14:24,320 --> 00:14:24,940
I hear something.

274
00:14:24,940 --> 00:14:32,720
What the hell was that?

275
00:14:32,800 --> 00:14:34,000
Some kind of shockwave.

276
00:14:34,680 --> 00:14:35,940
We got another one coming.

277
00:14:36,600 --> 00:14:37,220
Hit the deck!

278
00:14:45,360 --> 00:14:51,880
What is that thing on her back?

279
00:14:51,880 --> 00:14:55,600
A pirarucu lives in the rivers of South America.

280
00:14:55,840 --> 00:14:57,880
It is the world's largest freshwater fish.

281
00:14:57,900 --> 00:14:58,600
Like the Amazon?

282
00:15:00,300 --> 00:15:02,720
How did you get all the way there and back so quick?

283
00:15:03,300 --> 00:15:06,660
I have the ability to fly at an airspeed of Mach 24.

284
00:15:07,200 --> 00:15:09,640
Moving to Mach 24, considering other variables,

285
00:15:09,900 --> 00:15:11,980
that's 30,000 kilometers per hour.

286
00:15:12,020 --> 00:15:13,660
Well, since she brought it all the way here,

287
00:15:13,760 --> 00:15:15,100
let's clean that fish, too.

288
00:15:15,360 --> 00:15:16,800
It'd make a great side dish.

289
00:15:16,800 --> 00:15:19,120
I wonder if something like that is even edible.

290
00:15:21,880 --> 00:15:23,740
All right, Sagada.

291
00:15:23,940 --> 00:15:25,480
What's got your panties in a twist?

292
00:15:26,120 --> 00:15:27,520
Well, Mikiko...

293
00:15:27,520 --> 00:15:29,340
These are the specs on Icarus.

294
00:15:29,660 --> 00:15:30,660
That's correct.

295
00:15:30,920 --> 00:15:31,600
Her maximum speed is...

296
00:15:31,600 --> 00:15:32,960
Kind of a waste, isn't it?

297
00:15:34,080 --> 00:15:36,900
An angel with seemingly unlimited power.

298
00:15:37,680 --> 00:15:40,580
I mean, she's faster than the world's top fighter jets.

299
00:15:43,900 --> 00:15:46,180
But she calls herself pet class.

300
00:15:47,100 --> 00:15:47,900
Give me a break.

301
00:15:49,700 --> 00:15:50,660
Let's eat!

302
00:15:50,660 --> 00:15:50,720
Let's eat!

303
00:15:51,880 --> 00:15:52,380
Killers!

304
00:15:52,560 --> 00:15:54,080
You actually made some real curry!

305
00:15:54,740 --> 00:15:56,940
Shocking as it may sound, Icarus made it.

306
00:15:57,020 --> 00:15:57,620
That's awesome.

307
00:15:58,140 --> 00:16:00,180
You tried your best and it really shows, too.

308
00:16:00,340 --> 00:16:01,000
Thanks a lot.

309
00:16:07,220 --> 00:16:08,340
This is the best.

310
00:16:09,480 --> 00:16:11,140
It's just like Mom used to make.

311
00:16:11,620 --> 00:16:12,060
Beautiful.

312
00:16:12,460 --> 00:16:13,800
The sweetness...

313
00:16:13,800 --> 00:16:14,400
Hold up.

314
00:16:14,480 --> 00:16:15,500
It's just meat and potatoes.

315
00:16:16,160 --> 00:16:17,400
And I think I taste sugar.

316
00:16:17,920 --> 00:16:19,480
It doesn't make any difference.

317
00:16:19,480 --> 00:16:22,440
Meat and potatoes are the basic ingredients of curry, right?

318
00:16:22,440 --> 00:16:24,400
No, I'm pretty sure that's curry.

319
00:16:26,500 --> 00:16:28,460
Yeah, it wasn't that funny, Sahara.

320
00:16:28,460 --> 00:16:29,900
I know, sorry.

321
00:16:29,900 --> 00:16:35,340
It's just, ever since Icarus showed up, it seems like there's always something to laugh at.

322
00:16:35,460 --> 00:16:37,620
I guess she didn't do this to our dinner on purpose.

323
00:16:38,660 --> 00:16:39,140
Pardon?

324
00:16:39,700 --> 00:16:40,180
Master?

325
00:16:40,600 --> 00:16:43,260
I am curious as to what you were laughing at.

326
00:16:43,260 --> 00:16:45,140
What do you mean?

327
00:16:45,360 --> 00:16:47,140
We're just laughing to have a good time.

328
00:16:47,260 --> 00:16:48,320
Isn't that reason enough?

329
00:16:48,680 --> 00:16:50,060
Having a good time?

330
00:16:51,140 --> 00:16:53,100
You mean, like fun?

331
00:16:57,100 --> 00:16:58,340
Nothing out of the ordinary.

332
00:16:58,340 --> 00:17:19,060
What are you, really?

333
00:17:19,060 --> 00:17:29,580
If you didn't hear me, I'm asking you what you are.

334
00:17:35,580 --> 00:17:38,840
I am a pet class Angeloid, type Alpha.

335
00:17:39,180 --> 00:17:40,420
Don't play dumb with me.

336
00:17:40,700 --> 00:17:46,160
Would anything that's just a pet have the need to, or be designed to, catch a gigantic fish alive,

337
00:17:46,160 --> 00:17:51,600
or fly at Mach 24, but at the same time, your computational ability is that of a baby.

338
00:17:51,940 --> 00:17:53,980
It also seems that your emotions are limited.

339
00:17:55,620 --> 00:17:58,560
Both completely perfect and completely imperfect.

340
00:18:00,080 --> 00:18:02,040
Just what are you?

341
00:18:05,380 --> 00:18:06,080
Answer me.

342
00:18:06,400 --> 00:18:07,800
Why have you sought out Tomoki?

343
00:18:07,920 --> 00:18:09,240
There has to be a reason.

344
00:18:12,080 --> 00:18:13,220
I do not know.

345
00:18:13,220 --> 00:18:16,720
I am unaware of what my purpose should be on this world.

346
00:18:16,920 --> 00:18:17,660
What do you mean?

347
00:18:18,200 --> 00:18:19,520
I stay by his side.

348
00:18:20,120 --> 00:18:25,160
Those are the orders Master gave me, and that is the only reason I have for remaining here with him.

349
00:18:25,600 --> 00:18:30,820
But in doing so, I am constantly causing him great distress, and I do not know how to make that stop.

350
00:18:33,500 --> 00:18:38,440
Much like how Master is angry with me right now, I am sure you have noticed this.

351
00:18:38,440 --> 00:18:41,860
I can't help but wonder if I were to leave Master's side.

352
00:18:42,420 --> 00:18:43,840
Maybe he would be better off.

353
00:18:45,840 --> 00:18:48,800
She doesn't have the first clue what she is any more than I do.

354
00:18:49,180 --> 00:18:51,000
So the problem becomes a question.

355
00:18:51,620 --> 00:18:53,120
Who sent Icarus to Tomoki?

356
00:18:53,120 --> 00:18:57,980
You should just do your best to have fun.

357
00:18:58,940 --> 00:18:59,240
Hmm?

358
00:18:59,640 --> 00:19:02,880
You should just do what you can to have a good time while you're around Tomoki.

359
00:19:06,160 --> 00:19:10,520
And then you pray that the day you two part never comes.

360
00:19:10,520 --> 00:19:23,060
Wind check, positioning check, weather conditions good.

361
00:19:23,400 --> 00:19:25,160
Now hit the sky, Tomoki!

362
00:19:25,220 --> 00:19:27,520
Aren't you the one supposed to be doing this insanity?

363
00:19:29,000 --> 00:19:30,260
Everything's an experience.

364
00:19:30,660 --> 00:19:31,420
Now go!

365
00:19:33,020 --> 00:19:33,880
Take off!

366
00:19:33,880 --> 00:19:34,420
You're a demon!

367
00:19:34,760 --> 00:19:36,060
You're a devil incarnate!

368
00:19:36,920 --> 00:19:39,740
Say if you will, this is repayment for all the homework help.

369
00:19:39,740 --> 00:19:41,920
Tomoki, don't let go!

370
00:19:42,140 --> 00:19:44,720
A fall like that will take him weeks to recover from.

371
00:19:45,080 --> 00:19:48,300
I guess my calculations are still a tad off, which means that...

372
00:19:48,300 --> 00:19:48,480
Pardon me.

373
00:19:48,800 --> 00:19:50,220
May I ask you a question?

374
00:19:50,940 --> 00:19:51,800
What is it?

375
00:19:52,360 --> 00:19:54,920
You see, I was just wondering if...

376
00:19:54,920 --> 00:19:57,960
if my Master's Master has fun when he is around Master.

377
00:19:58,540 --> 00:19:58,840
Hmm?

378
00:19:59,680 --> 00:20:04,820
I've been trying, but I still don't think I really understand what this word called fun means.

379
00:20:05,440 --> 00:20:06,960
But I guess...

380
00:20:06,960 --> 00:20:07,580
But what?

381
00:20:07,580 --> 00:20:09,980
When I am with Master...

382
00:20:09,980 --> 00:20:14,080
My heart feels lighter.

383
00:20:14,800 --> 00:20:18,160
Like it's trying to fly right out of my chest all on its own.

384
00:20:19,000 --> 00:20:20,180
That makes sense.

385
00:20:23,020 --> 00:20:25,100
Then you should make that your homework assignment.

386
00:20:25,760 --> 00:20:28,400
And I will expect you to turn in a report to me in one day.

387
00:20:29,060 --> 00:20:29,460
Understood.

388
00:20:29,460 --> 00:20:32,720
I'm back.

389
00:20:34,840 --> 00:20:36,220
And I'm exhausted.

390
00:20:36,560 --> 00:20:39,280
I'm glad you walked away from that fall with just cuts and bruises.

391
00:20:43,880 --> 00:20:46,220
You brought the watermelon back with you?

392
00:20:46,360 --> 00:20:46,860
Correct.

393
00:20:46,860 --> 00:20:49,420
Well, in that case, I suppose we should have some.

394
00:20:51,340 --> 00:20:53,640
You really like that watermelon, don't you?

395
00:20:58,960 --> 00:21:00,460
At least our homework's done.

396
00:21:00,460 --> 00:21:04,700
Yeah, and our impromptu camping trip was a whole lot of fun, too.

397
00:21:08,280 --> 00:21:10,600
It gets funnier every time I look at it.

398
00:21:11,600 --> 00:21:12,640
Tell me, Master.

399
00:21:13,060 --> 00:21:15,840
Do you have a good time when I am here with you?

400
00:21:16,240 --> 00:21:17,680
Boy, do I ever, Icarus.

401
00:21:17,900 --> 00:21:20,640
There's never a dull moment with you around, that's for sure.

402
00:21:20,640 --> 00:21:25,500
But before we get started tonight, folks, I've got a question.

403
00:21:25,680 --> 00:21:27,880
What's the deal with these new HDTVs?

404
00:21:28,240 --> 00:21:30,280
What are you scribbling on over there, Icarus?

405
00:21:30,520 --> 00:21:32,500
I am writing on my homework.

406
00:21:32,500 --> 00:21:36,220
And now we're going to be broadcasting in all digital formats,

407
00:21:36,660 --> 00:21:38,580
which means you're going to get a technical question.

408
00:21:38,580 --> 00:21:41,180
In high depth, in your home.

409
00:21:42,500 --> 00:21:44,100
I see myself every day.

410
00:21:44,100 --> 00:22:14,080
I see myself every day.

411
00:22:14,100 --> 00:22:44,080
I see myself every day.

412
00:22:44,100 --> 00:23:14,080
I see myself every day.

413
00:23:14,100 --> 00:23:18,820
I see myself every day.

414
00:23:22,940 --> 00:23:24,320
The stupid screws are loose.

415
00:23:32,380 --> 00:23:34,780
Would you stop messing with the toilet seat?

416
00:23:34,780 --> 00:23:39,980
Next time, Love and Triangles Revisited.

